{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '510,555p' src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc | nl -ba -v 510 && sed -n '1240,1270p' src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc | nl -ba -v 1240\"","aggregated_output":"   510\t  \"The engine's composition for `dao.stream.waitset/check`: the whole\n   511\t   resolver contract in one value, both functions synchronous and pure over\n   512\t   the immutable resources table. Neither touches a transport -- the\n   513\t   library polls, the engine maps.\n   514\t\n   515\t   `:resolve` maps one whole parked entry to its live handle plus the\n   516\t   cursor to read from -- or the value to append -- out of the VM's\n   517\t   `:resources`. The cursor is re-resolved on every round even when an\n   518\t   earlier round baked a value into the entry: another waiter on the same\n   519\t   cursor-ref may have advanced the cell since. `:advance` commits a woken\n   520\t   reader's successor -- or recovery -- cursor to its cell before later\n   521\t   entries resolve, so a shared cursor-ref advances within the round.\"\n   522\t  {:resolve (fn [resources entry]\n   523\t              (if-let [cursor-ref (:cursor-ref entry)]\n   524\t                (let [cursor-data (get resources (:id cursor-ref))]\n   525\t                  {:stream (or (:stream entry)\n   526\t                               (get resources (:stream-id cursor-data)))\n   527\t                   :cursor (:cursor cursor-data)})\n   528\t                {:stream (or (:stream entry) (get resources (:stream-id entry)))\n   529\t                 :value (:datom entry)}))\n   530\t   :advance (fn [resources entry cursor]\n   531\t              (let [cursor-id (:id (:cursor-ref entry))]\n   532\t                (if cursor-id\n   533\t                  (assoc-in resources [cursor-id :cursor] cursor)\n   534\t                  resources)))})\n   535\t\n   536\t\n   537\t;; =============================================================================\n   538\t;; Lift and lower: the portable encoding a linked slice crosses in\n   539\t;; (yin.vm.linker.md section 7.3, acts 1 and 4; UCF section 7.5.1)\n   540\t;; =============================================================================\n   541\t\n   542\t(defn- non-portable!\n   543\t  [kind data]\n   544\t  (fail \"Value is not portable\"\n   545\t        (merge data {:yin.k/status :yin.k/non-portable, :yin.k/kind kind})))\n   546\t\n   547\t\n   548\t(defn- scalar?\n   549\t  [x]\n   550\t  (or (nil? x) (boolean? x) (number? x) (string? x) (keyword? x)\n   551\t      (symbol? x)))\n   552\t\n   553\t\n   554\t(defn- encode-primitive\n   555\t  \"A host function as UCF 7.5.2's primitive marker: its one name in\n  1240\t   envelope and, appended, polls on as a `:link-response`; an `:install`\n  1241\t   waits for its install. Returns `[state waiting woken]`.\"\n  1242\t  [state entry]\n  1243\t  (case (:reason entry)\n  1244\t    :link-request\n  1245\t    (let [entry' (module/append-link-request (:resources state) entry)]\n  1246\t      (if (= :link-response (:reason entry'))\n  1247\t        (poll-link-response state entry')\n  1248\t        [state entry' nil]))\n  1249\t    :link-response (poll-link-response state entry)\n  1250\t    :install [state entry nil]))\n  1251\t\n  1252\t\n  1253\t(defn- poll-links\n  1254\t  \"Poll every link wait entry once, in wait-set order, and then step the\n  1255\t   install children. Returns the state with the still-waiting link\n  1256\t   entries appended to `others` and the woken ones queued.\"\n  1257\t  [state links others]\n  1258\t  (let [[state waiting woken]\n  1259\t        (reduce (fn [[state waiting woken] entry]\n  1260\t                  (let [[state w k] (poll-link-entry state entry)]\n  1261\t                    [state\n  1262\t                     (cond-> waiting w (conj w))\n  1263\t                     (cond-> woken k (conj k))]))\n  1264\t                [state [] []]\n  1265\t                links)]\n  1266\t    (-> state\n  1267\t        (assoc :wait-set (into (vec others) waiting))\n  1268\t        (update :ready-queue (fnil into []) woken)\n  1269\t        advance-installs)))\n  1270\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-27 15:20:36 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-27 22:20:36 +07\n\nP1 | [remote.cljc:119](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:119) | The facade accepts invented `{:handle … :position …}` entries. Parked VM waits instead use `:stream-id`, `:cursor-ref`, and private `:resources` ([semantic.cljc:106](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:106); [engine.cljc:522](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:522)). Nothing connects those states to this facade, so its round trips do not establish that a parked wait resumes. | Lift from actual parked entries and resources; lower into fresh resource entries and wait-set entries, preserving VM context.\n\nP1 | [remote.cljc:144](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:144) | Lift copies `:position` and declares `:dao.stream.remote/v1` without checking that the cursor is portable through the codec or that the source honors it. The acceptance tests pass an in-process cursor directly ([remote_test.cljc:94](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc:94)). | Check the profile before publishing UCF data and test a codec round trip of the kept cursor before resume and eviction.\n\nP1 | [remote.cljc:57](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:57) | Every lift uses `:yin.k/c-0` in a separate table. No frame-level assembly or lowering preserves two waiters sharing one cursor cell, as §7.5.3 and the §7.11 pending-state blocker require. | Mint and remap cells across the whole frame, then test shared and independent cells at the same position.\n\nAll seven named pending variants have lift and lower branches and individual round-trip tests. The new module requires only `dao.stream`; I found no circular require or network dependency in `yin.vm` core. I did not edit files or rerun suites.\n\nVerdict: REQUEST CHANGES\nSign-off: DENIED"}}
